<%- include('./partials/header.ejs') %>

    <!-- Privacy Policy Page -->
    <section class="legal-page privacy-policy-page">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="legal-container">
                <div class="legal-header">
                    <h1 class="legal-title fs-32 fw-700">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p class="legal-updated fs-16">Last updated: 1/22/2026</p>
                </div>

                <div class="legal-content">
                    <!-- Section 1 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">1. Introduction</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">This Privacy Policy describes how Rubitt ("Rubitt," "we," "us," or
                            "our") collects, uses, stores, and discloses personal information. By using Rubitt, you
                            agree to the practices described in this policy.</p>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Rubitt provides AI-powered study tools, including lecture
                            transcription, note generation, flashcards, quizzes, and tutoring features. This policy
                            applies to all users, including high-school and college students.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 2 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">2. Information We Collect</h2>

                        <h3 class="subsection-title fs-20 fw-600">2.1 Information You Provide</h3>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We collect information that you voluntarily submit through the
                            platform, including:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Account information (e.g., name, email address).</li>
                            <li>Lecture recordings.</li>
                            <li>Lecture transcripts.</li>
                            <li>Notes, flashcards, quizzes, study guides, and other user-generated study materials.</li>
                            <li>Text inputs and messages submitted to the AI tutor.</li>
                            <li>Uploaded documents (e.g., syllabi, files).</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 class="subsection-title fs-20 fw-600">2.2 Automatically Collected Information</h3>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We may collect technical and usage information, such as:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Device type, operating system, and app version.</li>
                            <li>IP address and general location.</li>
                            <li>Log data related to platform usage.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Specific analytics tools have not yet been implemented. This
                            policy will be updated once those tools are added.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 3 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We use personal information for the following purposes:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>To generate transcripts, notes, flashcards, quizzes, and other study materials.</li>
                            <li>To operate, maintain, and improve the platform.</li>
                            <li>To provide personalized study support.</li>
                            <li>To secure user accounts and prevent misuse.</li>
                            <li>To communicate service-related updates or support information.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16"><strong>We do not use personal information to train AI
                                models.</strong></p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 4 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">4. AI Processing of User Content</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">User content (including recordings, transcripts, and text inputs)
                            may be processed by third-party AI providers solely to generate the requested outputs. These
                            providers:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Do not retain user content after processing.</li>
                            <li>Do not use user content to train their models.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Rubitt deletes all lecture recordings immediately after
                            transcription is completed. Transcripts and generated study materials remain accessible in
                            the user's account until deleted under Rubitt's retention practices.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 5 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">5. Data Retention</h2>

                        <h3 class="subsection-title fs-20 fw-600">5.1 Lecture Recordings</h3>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Lecture recordings are deleted immediately after transcription and
                            are not stored.</p>

                        <h3 class="subsection-title fs-20 fw-600">5.2 Study Materials and Account Data</h3>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We store transcripts, notes, flashcards, quizzes, AI tutor
                            messages, and uploaded files so users may access them. A long-term retention schedule has
                            not yet been finalized; the policy will be updated once established.</p>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Users may delete their accounts at any time, and associated study
                            materials and personal data will be removed following account deletion.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 6 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">6. Data Security</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We implement administrative, technical, and physical safeguards
                            designed to protect personal information, including:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Encrypted transmission of data.</li>
                            <li>Secure cloud storage.</li>
                            <li>Access controls for authorized personnel only.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">No system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
                            protection.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 7 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">7. Sharing of Information</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We do not sell or share personal information with third parties
                            for advertising or marketing purposes. We may share information with service providers that
                            support the operation of Rubitt, such as:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Cloud hosting services.</li>
                            <li>AI processing vendors.</li>
                            <li>Authentication and infrastructure providers.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">These service providers may use personal information only as
                            necessary to perform services on our behalf and must protect it in accordance with this
                            policy.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 8 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">8. Children and Student Users</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Rubitt may be used by high-school students. We do not knowingly
                            collect personal information from children under 13 without required parental, or school
                            consent. We do not sell, share, or use student data for behavioral advertising or AI
                            training.</p>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Parents, guardians, or educational institutions may request
                            deletion of a minor's account and data.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 9 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">9. User Rights</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Users may:</p>
                        <ul class="legal-list fs-16">
                            <li>Access personal information associated with their account.</li>
                            <li>Correct or update account information.</li>
                            <li>Delete their account and associated data.</li>
                            <li>Request deletion of stored transcripts and materials.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">Upon account deletion, user data is removed from active systems.
                            Some technical, or security logs may be retained temporarily as required for operational
                            integrity.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 10 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">10. International Users</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">If you access Rubitt from outside the United States, your data may
                            be processed in the United States. By using the platform, you consent to such processing.
                            Users in jurisdictions with additional privacy rights (such as GDPR) may exercise those
                            rights as applicable.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 11 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Material changes
                            will be communicated through the platform or our website. Continued use of Rubitt after such
                            changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section 12 -->
                    <div class="legal-section">
                        <h2 class="section-title fs-24 fw-700">12. Contact Information</h2>
                        <p class="section-text fs-16">For privacy-related questions or requests, please contact us at:
                            [Insert final Rubitt privacy email here]</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <%- include('./partials/footer.ejs') %>